---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "Write-through on two ways with LRU: after a store miss and a store hit, the rank move comes last, after the write-through (cases 2, 8 and 6)."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A4: tag 0x02, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses | - | Set 2: no valid way holds tag 0x02. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Way 0 chosen: it is invalid (empty).
1.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
1.5 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (53) into r1.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x1A4: tag 0x06, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
2.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses | - | Set 2: no valid way holds tag 0x06. Miss.
2.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Way 1 chosen: it is invalid (empty).
2.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/1, tag 2/1, word 2/1/0, word 2/1/1, word 2/1/2, word 2/1/3, fills | - | Fill way 1 with line 0x1A0–0x1AF from memory.
2.5 | write | writePolicy | word 2/1/1 | - | Write 3 into word 1 of way 1.
2.6 | writeThrough | writePolicy | memory 0x1A4, writethroughs | - | Write-through: 3 also goes to memory at 0x1A4.
2.7 | rank | replacement | rank 2/0, rank 2/1 | - | LRU ranks in set 2: way 1 becomes 0 (most recent); way 0 is 1.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0A4: tag 0x02, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
3.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, stores, hits | - | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x02 matches. Hit.
3.3 | write | writePolicy | word 2/0/1 | - | Write 5 into word 1 of way 0.
3.4 | writeThrough | writePolicy | memory 0xA4, writethroughs | - | Write-through: 5 also goes to memory at 0x0A4.
3.5 | rank | replacement | rank 2/0, rank 2/1 | - | LRU ranks in set 2: way 0 becomes 0 (most recent); way 1 is 1.
